# DTF tier manifest: conda-cep47-future-timestamp-reject
#   (artifact-keeper#6529; fixed in 1.13.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem + conda.future-timestamp-reject
# (CONDA_FUTURE_TIMESTAMP=reject on the backend).
#
# THE BUG (#6529)  A conda upload whose builder `timestamp` (info/index.json)
# lies in the future was stored unchecked, although CEP 47 asks a channel
# server to reject or flag it. The default (warn) is covered by
# conda-cep47-indexed-timestamp; this tier runs the opt-in reject mode:
# a timestamp a day ahead is refused 400 naming the cause, nothing is stored
# or listed, and a current timestamp (and a seconds-valued one in the past)
# still uploads 201.
#
# The FIX case is RED on main before the fix (201) and GREEN with it.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem conda.future-timestamp-reject"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
COVERS="6529"
